CART548=own(548,'effective Cartier divisor in Remark5.2.2(a)','sur X','Current sur S; diplomatic sur X','Retain sur X in both layers.','rejected_source_correction','The main scan clearly prints X. Here X is explicitly the locally ringed topos (Sh(S_Zar),O_S). The correspondence between O_S-modules on the scheme and O_X-modules on this topos sends F to the same sheaf U↦F(U) on open subsets U⊂S; evaluation on those opens is its inverse. An effective Cartier divisor is an invertible ideal I⊂O_S locally generated by a non-zero-divisor. This correspondence preserves that exact inclusion, local generators, dual I^∨=O_S(D), and quotient O_S/I=O_D, giving precisely the displayed sequence0→O_S(−D)→O_S→O_D→0 in either description. Consequently the printed divisor on X has exactly the same mathematical meaning through this explicit identification. The previous current substitution S is unnecessary and is reverted.','amended')
