ACT553=own(553,'action induced by α:G→Aut_O(M)','fait opérer G sur underlined O^underlined m','Both attached layers say O^m','Current M; diplomatic O^m.','mathematical_source_correction','The representation specifies, on each object U, the action map G(U)×M(U)→M(U), (g,v)↦α_U(g)(v). The group and restriction identities follow directly from α being a sheaf homomorphism. The associated-module construction immediately following is P×^G M, using exactly that action. Section6.1 defines M=T(O^{n_1},…,O^{n_r}) as an arbitrary O-module; local freeness was an additional premise only for the earlier composition sentence, and no global basis of M was chosen. A chosen trivialization u:O^m→M transports the displayed action to O^m by (g,v)↦u^{-1}α(g)u(v), making the missing identification explicit, but it is absent from this assertion. For example on P¹, T(E)=E⊗O(1) gives M=O(1), with scalar action; Γ(O(1)) has basis X_0,X_1 whereas Γ(O) consists of constants, so no O≅M trivialization exists. Replacing O^m by M states exactly the already specified action and the module used in6.1.4. This reverses the earlier rejected correction.')
