f(17,'E_i in the first tensor factor of6.2.8','first determinant formula554','Main and witness565 distinguish the dotted i from digit1 in the adjacent expressions. For free bases e_a of E_1 and f_b of E_2, the map from (∧^{n_1}E_1)^{⊗n_2}⊗(∧^{n_2}E_2)^{⊗n_1} to ∧^{n_1n_2}(E_1⊗E_2) sends their ordered basis generators to the lexicographically ordered wedge of e_a⊗f_b. A basis change A,B multiplies both sides by det(A)^{n_2}det(B)^{n_1}, so these local maps glue. This proves the displayed right side for E_1⊗E_2, exactly as in the attached current correction; the unbound first factor E_i has no corresponding right-side determinant.',batch='551_555')
