CONS568=own(568,'parenthetical explanation that7.10.1 generalizes7.5','pour X=S, les flèches de(7.3.2)…','Same in both layers','Retain X=S in both layers; record the exact substitution into the explicitly cited diagram.','retained_reading','The parenthesis explicitly cites7.3.2, whose scheme parameter is X, so X=S is the correct substitution in that diagram. For the discrete valuation ring A, rank identifies K_•(S) with Z: finite modules decompose into free and torsion parts, and the sequence0→A→A→A/(π)→0 gives the torsion generator class0. Dimension identifies K_•(t) and K_•(s) with Z. The two pullbacks j* and i* send[A] to the one-dimensional residue-field class, so under these identifications both are the identity, and7.3.2 gives σ_S=id. Now take the TARGET Y=S in7.10.1 and g=f:X→S. Its horizontal maps become χ_t and χ_s, hence the commutative square says χ_sσ_X=χ_t, exactly7.5.1. Renaming the dummy X of7.3.2 to Y before this latter substitution is an identity relabeling of the same diagram. The printed parenthesis is correct; the proposed X→Y replacement is unnecessary.','confirmed retained reading');OWN[-1]['misprint']=False
