f(7,'x_i:S→X','first line574','Main and witness585 clearly print X. The preceding573 paragraph defines x_0,x_1 as sections of C→S, and the same574 sentence gives their base changes s→C_s. The exact square defining i_x is the base change of x:S→C by X×_S C→C, with i_x(z)=(z,x(f(z))). Thus the section named here has target C, as the attached current correction says; diplomatic retains X.',batch='571_575')
f(8,'E(x_1)−E(x_0) de K_•(X×_S C)','upper574, ambient group after the evaluated difference','Both scans print the product ambient group. Write π:X×_S C→X and i_x:X→X×_S C. The displayed definition E(x)=i_x^*E gives d=E(x_1)−E(x_0) in K_•(X). Since C→S is flat, π^* is defined, and π∘i_x=id_X gives i_x^*π^*=id by the stated transitivity of perfect pullbacks. Hence π^*:K_•(X)→K_•(X×_S C) is a canonical split embedding, and the printed ambient reading represents d by π^*d. Recovering it by i_{x_0}^* gives d exactly. Its generic restriction is d_t=E_t(x_{1t})−E_t(x_{0t}), and the specialization in7.3.1 gives σ(d_t)=i^*d=i^*i_{x_0}^*(π^*d). The sentence’s son image par7.3.1 refers to that preceding generic-fibre difference. Thus the printed ambient group and the subsequent displayed image are connected by explicit maps giving the exact same element; the proposed replacement is unnecessary.','reverted inferred-slip verdict','Retain the product ambient group in both layers; keep the split-embedding explanation in the apparatus only.',batch='571_575');D[-1]['misprint']=False
